From 585921fba8abca94aa0c48987058d82dbad18651 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:41:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [ActiveAE] Keep the back centre of 6.1 and 6.0 tracks for a
 receiver that has the speaker

ApplySettingsToFormat() resolves a multichannel track to the speakers of
"Number of channels", and none of those layouts has a back centre: the
back centre of a 6.1 track (Dolby Digital EX, DTS-ES decoded to PCM) is
mixed into the two back speakers (CAEChannelInfo::ResolveChannels()), and
with 7.1 set 8 channels are asked of the sink. A receiver set up for 6.1
says so in its ELD (speaker RC), and the HDMI codec of the kernel then
offers the CTA-861 allocations of its speakers: 6.1 is 0x0f (FL FR LFE
FC RL RR RC), 6.0 is 0x0e, and there is no allocation for 8 channels. The
ALSA sink falls back to the nearest map, 5.1 (0x0b), and the back centre
speaker of the receiver plays nothing.

Where the output declares a back centre speaker (CAEDeviceInfo::
m_channels, from the ELD as far as the channel maps carry it), "Number of
channels" is 7.0 or 7.1 and the track has a back centre beside one pair
of surrounds, the track is now resolved to those speakers with the back
centre (AE::PCM::SpeakersForBackCentre(), AEBackCentre.h): a 6.1 track
goes out in its 7 channels and the sink takes allocation 0x0f, a 6.0 one
in 6 and 0x0e. Within what goes out: the setting as the user set it, but
no more channels than the setting limited to the display may send (so a
7.1 setting on a display of 7 channels still gives 6.1 with its LFE).

Unchanged: every other track and output, a 3/1 track whose back centre is
its one surround channel (it is meant for both surround speakers), a track
with both side and back pairs, 5.1 or less set, passthrough, and the
fixed configuration. kodi.log says once, when it changes, what was done
with the back centre of a track ("goes to the back centre speaker that
the output declares", or why it is mixed into the back speakers).

Host test (TestAEBackCentre, 7 tests): with the change 7 of 7 pass; with
Kodi's behaviour in its place (the speakers as they are) 6 of them fail.
A harness with the sink's own choice of map (GetAlternateLayoutForm()
taken word for word, the allocations of the kernel for a 6.1 ELD):
before, 8 channels asked and allocation 0x0b; now 7 and 0x0f, and 6.0
gives 0x0e (2 of its 3 tests fail with Kodi's behaviour). Six mutants of
the rule, all caught. Not tried with a receiver.
